Before I started this years major Nethack game, I first investigated how 
I could achieve the most deadly weapons combo EVER. Frost Brand is 
generally considered the best all-round weapon, and I figured that a 
Samurai could best double-weapon it with a silver saber. So, finally I 
stand proudly on the upstairs of level 1, Roar the Shogun, at experience 
level 30, strength 18/**, dexterity 23, wearing a ring of free action 
and a +4 ring of increase damage, wielding the blessed rustproof +7 
Frost Brand in one hand and a blessed rustproof +7 silver saber in the 
other.

[Not without a bit of prehistory, though. Some may remember that I 
stuffed my totally unused /oWishing into my bag of holding and a 
/oCancellation shortly after. Problem was worse, though, because 7 
candles were in that exploding bag too, and only 4 remained in Mine 
Town. So I played a lot with magic traps, and about 90000 turns into the 
game, a leocrotta comes along with a wand of polymorph. Shortly after I 
had enough candles, and 12 blessed scrolls of charging that came in 
handy later. But in all this time, I could not generate a single wish 
with smoky potions, thrones or anything else, and a blessed magic lamp 
yielded a hostile Djinni. Grrr, now the RNG owes me!]

Anyway, IS that the most deadly weapons combo, or Is it Not? It was 
pretty deadly, I can tell you. Not many monsters are both cold and 
silver resistant. Being able to whack vampires in one stroke yields a 
LOT of potions of full healing and gain level. On the plane of Earth I 
was a bit concerned, because the earth elementals took a long time to 
die, 4-5 whacks most of the time. But I took it easy and patiently 
exterminated them all, while stocking up on potions because I was 
running low on holy water.

The plane of Air was EASY. I did not teleport the air elementals away, I 
MURDERED them. Actually, being swallowed only insured that I got a much 
better hit, three whacks and I am outta there. I never even got into the 
yellow (playing Qt/tiles) on my HP during the whole endgame.

I met an Archon on the Plane of Air. Some rounds of charm monster, and 
he's mine. It's true what they say, Archons are THE best pets. Not only 
was it loyal and stayed close, he was resistant to most things and 
really threw a good punch. A previous Archon pet was swallowed whole by 
a purple worm, three turn after I tamed him, so I genocided purple worms 
for good measure. I gave him my spare +2 Snickersnee, but he would not 
take my carefully prepared +5 gdsm. (I made it for him there on the 
Astral plane from gray dragon scales lying around. A bit scary, really, 
undressing totally on the Plane of Air, but everything was perfectly 
calm, not a monster in sight.) Funny though, early on the Astral Plane a 
Valkyrie named Gerda or something came along with the +5 Grayswandir, 
but the Archon would not swap. Stupid pet!

That Gerda had a potion of enlightenment (smoky) as well. I had gotten 
into a habit of blessing it, quaffing it and seeing my stats (i.e. NOT 
getting a djinni), so I did it this time as well. Truly, the RNG is Fair 
and Wise! A Djinni pops out, finally granting me a wish! I wished for a 
helm of brilliance, because I had not been able to obtain it earlier. 
Donned it removed the rest of my armor (now, on the ASTRAL PLANE, with 
all the monsters STILL LURKING, it is MORE SCARY), and enchanted it to 
+4. What surprised me was that with Int 22 (or was it Wis?) and explevel 
30, some spells that I am skilled at such as FoD are still at 30% fail. 
Samurais are probably not meant to do FoD, then.

The Astral Plane was EASY. Pestilence: two whacks, no illness. Wrong 
altar. On my way out, he managed to get me ill from two squares away, I 
wonder how. Death: one blessed rustproof +7 shuriken (I had a LONG 
preparation, remember), and just one whack. In one turn he took my Max 
HP down from 498 to 465, though. Wrong altar again. With this weapon 
combo and not bothering to kill lower vermin such as priests and angels, 
you can really move FAST on the Astral Plane. Insects are a blessing, 
because you can move faster through them than the bad monsters, and they 
have no chance of hitting. Finally I ate a few wafers of lembas in peace 
and quiet and was satiated when I met Famine: whack-o, he never even got 
me un-satiated. Right altar.

THIS IS JUST TOO EASY, I thought. Instead of offering, i dropped the 
amulet on the altar of Amaterasu Omikami, and went on a rampage. Lit the 
entire Astral Plane and killed everyone in sight. Then a thought struck 
me about the Riders: If you can't kill them, join them. So I figured I 
would have Death, Famine and Pestilence attend my ascension. After not a 
little bit of trouble, I rounded them up around the altar.

I struggled for a while to achieve the perfect tableau, and quickly read 
a couple of create monster while confused, to "fix" the scene. In this 
perfect setting, I finally offered the amulet:

